# cited-url-lint allowlist
# ========================
#
# Convention:
# - One entry per line
# - Bare path (e.g., docs/example.md) skips the entire file
# - allow-url:<url> skips a specific URL across all files
# - Lines starting with # are comments
# - Blank lines are ignored
#
# When to add an entry:
# - A URL requires authentication (e.g., private API docs, GitHub private repos)
# - A URL is behind Cloudflare or other anti-bot protection that blocks HEAD requests
# - A URL is known-good but the host is rate-limited or flaky
# - A URL is in a code block / example (not a real assertion) — prefer excluding the file instead
#
# Examples (commented out):
# allow-url:https://api.example.com/internal-docs  # requires auth
# docs/changelog/internal-migrations.md             # file contains internal-only links
